== About Me

I am a Ph.D. student in Applied Mathematics at Harvard University. My research
interests lie in high-dimensional statistics and machine learning theory,
random matrix theory, and distributed optimization. I am particularly
interested in developing precise mathematical characterizations of modern
learning and inference problems.

Before Harvard, I received my B.Sc. in Mathematics and Applied Mathematics
from the School of the Gifted Young at University of Science and Technology
of China (USTC).

== Education

- Harvard University: Ph.D. in Applied Mathematics, 2020-present. Advisor: Professor Yue M. Lu.
- University of Science and Technology of China: B.Sc. in Mathematics and Applied Mathematics, 2016-2020.
